<com:TContent ID="body">
<h1 id="ActiveHyperLink">TActiveHyperLink</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.1" />
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.ActiveControls.TActiveHyperLink" />

<p class="block-content">
The active control counterpart of <a href="?page=Controls.HyperLink">THyperLink</a>. It
renders the same <tt>&lt;a&gt;</tt> element and adds the ability to change the link
during a callback.
</p>

<h2>What updates during a callback</h2>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Property</th><th>Effect on the browser</th></tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>NavigateUrl</tt></td>
	<td>Rewrites the <tt>href</tt> attribute.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>Target</tt></td>
	<td>Rewrites the <tt>target</tt> attribute.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>Text</tt></td>
	<td>Replaces the content of the link.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>ImageUrl</tt></td>
	<td>Renders a fresh image and replaces the content of the link with it. Assigning an empty value sends nothing, so an image already shown cannot be removed this way.</td>
</tr>
</table>

<p class="block-content">
Each update is subject to <a href="?page=ActiveControls.Introduction#ClientSideUpdates">the five conditions for a client-side update</a>. <tt>Text</tt> and <tt>ImageUrl</tt> both
replace the same region, so the one assigned last is the one the user sees.
</p>

